course: dictionary
lesson: 6393
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one you need. Context means the words and sentences around a word. «Mummy, can you read me a story?» means your mother, because a child is talking to a parent.
explain: «The museum has a mummy from ancient Egypt, wrapped in cloth.» Here mummy means a dead body kept from rotting long ago. The words museum, ancient and Egypt are the clues. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence best?
explain: Mummy can also be a scary monster in a film or a story, a wrapped body that walks. If the sentence is about a spooky night and not a family, choose the spooky meaning.
fact: Mummy has more than one meaning, so check the context before you choose.
fact: In everyday life, a small child calls their mother «Mummy». In the USA they say «mommy».
fact: In history lessons, mummies tell us how ancient Egyptians lived and what they believed.
fact: «Maman» is French for mummy, and Louise Bourgeois made giant spider sculptures called Maman.
fact: A museum keeps important objects safe, including mummies, and shows them to everyone.
exercise: «Mummy, can you read me a story?» Who is Mummy here? | A spooky monster in a film | A museum guide | *Your mother | A dead body from ancient Egypt
exercise: «The museum has a mummy from ancient Egypt, wrapped in cloth.» What is a mummy here? | A spooky monster that walks | A small child | *A dead body kept from rotting long ago | A famous painting
exercise: Ravi says every mummy is a spooky monster. What should he do instead? | Skip every sentence with mummy in it forever | *Check the context, because mummy can mean mother, a dead body or a monster | Always use the spooky meaning | Ignore the sentence and guess
test: In «The Mariner had his Mummy's leave to paddle», who is Mummy? | A scary monster in a story | A spider sculpture | A dead body kept in a museum | *His mother
test: In «Maman, French for mummy», what does mummy mean? | A kind of spider | A wrapped body from Egypt | *A child's word for mother | A spooky monster that walks
exam: Which is the best way to find the meaning of mummy in an unknown sentence? | Guess the first meaning you think of | *Read the words around mummy and try each meaning in the sentence | Ask someone else to decide without thinking | Skip the sentence and never come back to it
